{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e4c1a0-velora-api-4f21-9c0d-2a1b3c4d5e6f",
    "name": "Velora Hospital Management API",
    "description": "Velora API \u2014 Django REST Framework, session authentication + CSRF.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Start the backend: uvicorn config.asgi:application --port 8000\n2. Run 'Get CSRF token', then 'Login' (folder 0). Postman's cookie jar keeps the session automatically.\n3. Everything else just works \u2014 the collection auto-attaches X-CSRFToken on POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE and refreshes it after login (Django rotates it).\n\nDemo accounts (seed_demo): admin/head/doctor/nurse/guard/accounts @velora.com \u2014 password123.\nClinical writes (e.g. creating patients) are role-scoped: use doctor@velora.com or nurse@velora.com. Admin sees staff/reports/billing.\n\nTip: list requests auto-capture IDs (patient_id, department_id, nurse_id, ...) into collection variables used by the create/detail requests. Run lists before creates.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Attach the CSRF token header automatically on unsafe methods.",
          "const unsafe = [\"POST\", \"PUT\", \"PATCH\", \"DELETE\"];",
          "if (unsafe.includes(pm.request.method.toUpperCase())) {",
          "  let token = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"csrf_token\");",
          "  if (!token) { try { token = pm.cookies.get(\"velora_csrftoken\"); } catch (e) {} }",
          "  if (token) { pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: \"X-CSRFToken\", value: token }); }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// keep HTTP status visible in results"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
